    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Regulate fuel to a maximum of one‑quarter tank. This level prevents spillage during transit and complies with most interstate bike transport regulations. Drain excess fuel if necessary, seal the tank vent, and record the exact reading in the checklist, labeling it under ‘bike transport interstate’ for compliance verification.</p>
