      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Seorahi Kushinagar</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p>The original registration certificate (RC) is an essential document that confirms the ownership of the bike. To simplify the transportation process, it is advisable to obtain a self-attested photocopy of the RC.</p>

	<p>Proof of Vehicle Usage (PUC) is a certificate issued by local authorities, indicating that the bike has been inspected for emissions and safety standards. It is mandatory to present a valid PUC while transporting a motorcycle. Ensure that the PUC has less than 30 days before its expiry date for a smooth transportation process.</p>

	<p>Insurance is crucial for bike transportation as it covers any potential damage or accidents during transit. Ensure that you have a valid insurance certificate for your bike. It should cover both the source and destination points. Special mention should be made regarding 100% declared-value marine transit insurance.</p>

	<p>The Indian Bicycle Association (IBA) is a recognized organization for bike transportation in India. To ensure a secure transportation process, obtain an IBA-approved consignment bill of lading. This document serves as a contract between the transporter and the owner, detailing all the necessary information, such as bike details, transportation charges, and pickup and delivery dates.</p>

	<p>Select a reliable courier company for bike transportation. As a customer, you should ensure that the company is registered and has a valid trade license. Request the company to provide their registration details, such as GST number and business address.</p>

	<p>To prevent any dispute regarding the bike's condition upon delivery, it is advisable to obtain a vehicle condition report from the transporter. This report will detail the current condition of your bike, including photos and a written description. It will help to establish the bike's initial condition before transportation.</p>

	<p>In some cases, it is mandatory to obtain approval from the Regional Transport Office (RTO) for bike transportation. Ensure that you have obtained the necessary approval for the chosen route. This approval certificate will verify that the transportation process complies with the local transportation regulations.</p>

