      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Seorahi Kushinagar</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its destination, the delivery hand‑over must confirm that the vehicle’s condition matches the state recorded at pickup. The process is carried out in daylight to ensure clear visibility and consists of three core steps: a condition re‑inspection, odometer verification, and a signed condition sign‑off.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Daylight condition re‑inspection against pickup photos</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Position the vehicle in a well‑lit area, preferably under natural sunlight, to eliminate shadows that could hide surface damage.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Open the pickup photo dossier and compare each angle (front, rear, sides, top, and close‑ups of any pre‑existing dents or scratches).</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Inspect the bodywork, chrome, plastics, and tyres for new scratches, dents, or cracks that were not present in the original images.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Check the condition of accessories (mirrors, luggage racks, windshields) and verify that they remain securely attached.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Document any discrepancies with timestamped photographs and note them on the hand‑over checklist.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>

  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer verification against the LR bilty</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Read the odometer reading on the instrument cluster and record it on the hand‑over form.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Retrieve the LR (Logistics Receipt) bilty, which contains the mileage logged at the point of pickup.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the current reading with the pickup mileage; the difference should reflect the distance travelled during transit only.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If the mileage exceeds the expected range, investigate possible causes (e.g., detours, additional test rides) and obtain an explanatory note from the driver.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Sign off on the odometer check once the reading is verified as accurate.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>

  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed condition sign‑off</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both the receiver (customer or authorized representative) and the delivery agent review the inspection findings together.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The receiver confirms that the vehicle’s condition matches the pickup documentation and that the odometer reading is correct.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Each party signs the condition report, acknowledging acceptance of the vehicle in its current state.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>A copy of the signed report is provided to the receiver, while the original is retained by the logistics team for record‑keeping and future dispute resolution.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>
</ul>

<p>Completing these steps ensures transparency, protects both the logistics provider and the customer, and creates a reliable audit trail for any post‑delivery claims.</p></div>
